data/corpus/passages/*.json

    Extracted passages from books distributed by Project Gutenberg
    (https://www.gutenberg.org). The underlying works are in the public domain in
    the United States. Each passage file records its source ebook id, source URL,
    the SHA-256 of the exact book file it was cut from, and the rights statement
    Project Gutenberg published with that file.

    Project Gutenberg's own trademark licence applies to files that carry the
    Project Gutenberg header. The extraction step strips that header and footer,
    which -- per Project Gutenberg's terms -- means the resulting text may be used
    freely as a public-domain work, without the Project Gutenberg trademark and
    without the associated licence terms. We keep the provenance record anyway,
    because attribution is a research requirement here regardless of what the
    licence compels.

    Works whose United States public-domain status is not clear are out of scope
    for this corpus; see docs/corpus-rights.md.

data/slop_lexicon.yaml

    Terms and constructions are attributed per entry group in the file itself.
    Groups marked `source: curated:project` are this project's own additions and
    carry no external authority -- they are hypotheses, and plan.md §12 governs
    how they must be treated.
